From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:02:50 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm: allow the SSO driver to be built on MIPS

The Serial Shift Output controller is not a Lightning Mountain
peculiarity. Intel's GRX500 family carries the same block, at the same
register offsets, with the same two clock rates and the same 24/5/3
pin grouping -- close enough that the vendor's own GRX500 driver and
this one are two forks of one source file rather than two
implementations that happen to agree.

LGM is an x86 part, so depends on X86 was right when it was written and
simply never contemplated a second user. GRX500 is MIPS, and the symbol
is not selectable there at all: nothing else in the entry stands in the
way, since GPIOLIB, LEDS_CLASS, MFD_SYSCON and OF are all available and
already listed.

Nothing in the driver is architecture specific. It reaches the block
through a syscon regmap and a pair of clocks and touches no x86
facility. Widening the list rather than deleting it keeps the entry in
the shape its neighbour LEDS_BCM63138 uses, where the arch list names
the platforms the hardware is known to exist on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig b/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig
index bdcb7377cd4e..28b5f512b7ce 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ config LEDS_BCM63138
 
 config LEDS_LGM
        tristate "LED support for LGM SoC series"
-       depends on X86 || COMPILE_TEST
+       depends on X86 || MIPS || COMPILE_TEST
        depends on GPIOLIB && LEDS_CLASS && MFD_SYSCON && OF
        help
          This option enables support for LEDs connected to GPIO lines on
